{"kind":"multiple","metadata":{"title":"Molecule of the Month: Myoglobin","timestamp":"2025-11-08T10:21:46.509Z","version":"1"},"snapshots":[{"root":{"kind":"root","children":[{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1mbn.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":"ligand"},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"ref":"ligand","children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"orange"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":155,"label_atom_id":"FE"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"yellow"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":154}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"blue"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"surface","surface_type":"gaussian"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#ff0303"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"surfopa"}]},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"line"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"element-symbol"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"lineopa"}]},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"cartoon"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"secondary-structure"}}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"label_opacity":0,"label_background_color":"grey","snapshot_key":"intro"},"ref":"start-story","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"Start story","position":[13.5,-4,7.7],"label_size":8}}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"camera","params":{"position":[13.5,21.1,-56.02242622983463],"target":[13.5,21.1,7.7],"up":[0,1,0]}}]},"metadata":{"key":"first-slide","title":"Introduction","description":"# Introduction\n\nA story based on the orginal [first Molecule of the Month](https://pdb101.rcsb.org/motm/1) made by David Goodsell in January 2000.\n\n*This story includes short audio commentaries to guide you through the structures.  \nFor the best experience, please keep your sound on or use headphones.*","linger_duration_ms":5000,"transition_duration_ms":1000},"animation":{"kind":"animation","children":[{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"start-story","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":1,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}}],"params":{},"custom":{"molstar_trackball":{"name":"spin","params":{"speed":-0.05}}}}},{"root":{"kind":"root","custom":{"molstar_on_load_markdown_commands":{"play-audio":"AudioMOM1_A.mp3"}},"children":[{"kind":"canvas","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_postprocessing":{"enable_outline":false}}},{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1mbn.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":"ligand"},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"ref":"ligand","children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"orange"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":155,"label_atom_id":"FE"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"yellow"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":154}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"blue"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"surface","surface_type":"gaussian"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#ff0303"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"surfopa"}]},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"line"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"element-symbol"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"lineopa"}]},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"cartoon"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"secondary-structure"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color_from_source","params":{"schema":"all_atomic","category_name":"atom_site","field_name":"type_symbol","palette":{"kind":"categorical","colors":{"C":"#FFFFFF","N":"#CCE6FF","O":"#FFCCCC","S":"#FFE680"}}}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"cpkopa1"}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":155}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":8421504,"saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":0.8}}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"cpkopa2"}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"tooltip":"Click for next part","label_opacity":0,"label_background_color":"grey","snapshot_key":"whale"},"ref":"next","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","position":[13.5,-4,7.7],"text":"Next Scene →","label_color":"white","label_size":5},"ref":"next_label"}]},{"kind":"camera","params":{"position":[13.5,21.1,-56.02242622983463],"target":[13.5,21.1,7.7],"up":[0,1,0]}}]},"metadata":{"key":"intro","title":"Molecule of the Month: Myoglobin","description":"# Molecule of the Month: Myoglobin\n\nMyoglobin was the first protein to have its atomic structure determined, revealing how it stores oxygen in muscle cells.\n\n---\n\n## The First Protein Structure\n\nAny discussion of protein structure must necessarily begin with **myoglobin**, because it is where the science of protein structure began. After years of arduous work, *John Kendrew* and his coworkers determined the atomic structure of myoglobin, laying the foundation for an era of biological understanding.\n\nYou can take a close look at this protein structure yourself, in **PDB entry [1mbn](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/1MBN)**. You will be amazed—just like the world was in 1960—at the beautiful intricacy of this protein.\n\n---\n\n## Myoglobin and Muscles\n\n[Myoglobin](!query%3Dchain%20A%26lang%3Dpymol%26action%3Dhighlight%2Cfocus) is a **small, bright red protein**. It is very common in muscle cells and gives meat much of its red color. Its job is to **store oxygen**, for use when muscles are hard at work.\n\nTo do this, it uses a special chemical tool to capture slippery oxygen molecules: a **[heme group](!query%3Dresn%20HEM%26lang%3Dpymol%26action%3Dhighlight%2Cfocus)**. Heme is a disk-shaped molecule with a hole in the center that is perfect for holding an iron ion. The iron then forms a strong interaction with the **[oxygen molecule](!query%3Dresn%20OH%26lang%3Dpymol%26action%3Dhighlight%2Cfocus)**. As you can see in the structure, the heme group is held tightly in a deep pocket on one side of the protein.\n\n---\n\n## Visualizing Protein Structure\n\nWhen the structure of myoglobin was solved, it posed a great challenge. The structure is so complex that **new methods** needed to be developed to display and understand it.\n\n- *John Kendrew* used a huge wire model to build the structure based on the experimental electron density.  \n- Then, the artist *Irving Geis* was employed to create a picture of myoglobin for a prominent article in *Scientific American*.  \n- Computer graphics were still many years in the future, so he created this illustration entirely by hand—one atom at a time.  \n\nYou can learn more about the work of Irving Geis at the **[Geis Archive on PDB-101](https://pdb101.rcsb.org/learn/GeisArchive)**.\n\n![Alt Text](https://cdn.rcsb.org/pdb101/motm/1/1-Myoglobin-geis-0218-myoglobin.png)\n\n*Illustration of myoglobin by Irving Geis. You can learn more about this painting at the Geis Archive on PDB-101.  \nUsed with permission from the Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Copyright 2015.*","linger_duration_ms":45000,"transition_duration_ms":500},"animation":{"kind":"animation","children":[{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"lineopa","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":0,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"ligand","start_ms":22000,"duration_ms":10000,"frequency":6,"alternate_direction":true,"property":["custom","molstar_representation_params","emissive"],"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"cpkopa1","duration_ms":5000,"start_ms":40000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"cpkopa2","duration_ms":5000,"start_ms":40000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"next","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":43000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}}],"params":{},"custom":{"molstar_trackball":{"name":"spin","params":{"speed":-0.05}}}}},{"root":{"kind":"root","custom":{"molstar_on_load_markdown_commands":{"play-audio":"AudioMOM1_B.mp3"}},"children":[{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1mbn.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"transform","params":{"translation":[-30,0,0]},"ref":"whalex"},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color_from_source","params":{"schema":"all_atomic","category_name":"atom_site","field_name":"type_symbol","palette":{"kind":"categorical","colors":{"C":"#FFFFFF","N":"#CCE6FF","O":"#FFCCCC","S":"#FFE680"}}}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"auth_seq_id":155}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":8421504,"saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":0.8}}}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"label_opacity":1,"label_attachment":"top-center","label_show_tether":true,"label_tether_length":1},"ref":"prims","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"whale","position":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":8},"label_size":10}}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"label_opacity":0},"ref":"startres","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"★","label_offset":4,"position":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":12,"atom_id":96},"label_size":5}},{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"★","label_offset":4,"position":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":140,"auth_atom_id":"NZ"},"label_size":5}},{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"★","label_offset":4,"position":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":87,"auth_atom_id":"NZ"},"label_size":5}}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":[{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":12},{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":140},{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":87}]},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"surface","surface_type":"gaussian"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"emissive":0,"ignoreLight":true}},"ref":"scharged","children":[{"kind":"color_from_source","params":{"schema":"all_atomic","category_name":"atom_site","field_name":"type_symbol","palette":{"kind":"categorical","colors":{"C":"#FFFFFF","N":"#CCE6FF","O":"#FFCCCC","S":"#FFE680"}}}}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1pmb.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"transform","params":{"matrix":[0.4634187130865737,-0.7131589697034304,0.5259728687171936,0,-0.22944227902330105,-0.6698811108214233,-0.7061273127008398,0,0.8559202154942049,0.2065522332899299,-0.4740643150728161,0,-52.54880970106205,37.49099778180445,-6.133850309914719,1]},"ref":"pig"},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color_from_source","params":{"schema":"all_atomic","category_name":"atom_site","field_name":"type_symbol","palette":{"kind":"categorical","colors":{"C":"#FFFFFF","N":"#CCE6FF","O":"#FFCCCC","S":"#FFE680"}}}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"C","auth_seq_id":154}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"ignoreLight":true}},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":8421504,"saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":0.8}}}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"label_opacity":1,"label_attachment":"top-center","label_show_tether":true,"label_tether_length":1},"ref":"labelpig","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","text":"pig","position":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":8},"label_size":10}}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"tooltip":"Click for next part","label_opacity":0,"label_background_color":"grey","snapshot_key":"oxygen"},"ref":"next","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","position":[-18.9,-4,7.3],"text":"Next Scene →","label_color":"white","label_size":5},"ref":"next_label"}]},{"kind":"camera","params":{"position":[-23.08970080716038,-71.46315736749679,-50.381462275324324],"target":[-18.9,21.1,7.3],"up":[0,0.5,-0.8]}}]},"metadata":{"key":"whale","title":"Myoglobin and Whales","description":"# Myoglobin and Whales\n\nIf you look at John Kendrew's PDB file, you'll notice that the myoglobin he used was taken \nfrom sperm whale muscles. Whales and dolphin have a great need for myoglobin, so that they can \nstore extra oxygen for use in their deep undersea dives. Typically, they have about 30 \ntimes more than in animals that live on land. A recent study revealed that a few special \nmodifications are needed to make this possible.\n\nComparing whale myoglobin (PDB entry [1mbn](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/1mbn)) with \npig myoglobin (PDB entry [1pmb](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/1pmb)), we find that there are \nseveral mutations that add extra positively-charged amino acids to the surface. Marine animals typically have these extra charges on \nthe surface of their myoglobin to help repel neighboring molecules and prevent aggregation when myoglobin is at \nhigh concentrations.","linger_duration_ms":41000,"transition_duration_ms":500},"animation":{"kind":"animation","children":[{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"vec3","target_ref":"whalex","duration_ms":10000,"start_ms":16000,"property":"translation","start":[-30,0,0],"end":[-60,0,0]}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"startres","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":20000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"transform_matrix","target_ref":"pig","duration_ms":5000,"start_ms":18000,"property":"matrix","translation_start":[-82.54880970106205,37.49099778180445,-6.133850309914719],"translation_end":[-52.54880970106205,37.49099778180445,-6.133850309914719]}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"labelpig","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":18000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"next","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":38000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"scharged","start_ms":20000,"duration_ms":6000,"frequency":6,"alternate_direction":true,"property":["custom","molstar_representation_params","emissive"],"start":0,"end":1}}],"params":{},"custom":{"molstar_trackball":{"name":"spin","params":{"speed":-0.05}}}}},{"root":{"kind":"root","custom":{"molstar_on_load_markdown_commands":{"play-audio":"AudioMOM1_C.mp3"}},"children":[{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1mbo.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"transform","params":{"matrix":[-0.8334619943964441,-0.512838061396133,-0.20576353166796402,0,-0.20145089001561267,0.628743285359846,-0.7510655776229758,0,0.5145474196737698,-0.5845332204089626,-0.6273453801378679,0,11.864847328611186,-1.5261713438028912,23.638919347623467,1]}},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"C","auth_seq_id":155}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":14134100,"saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":1}}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"D","auth_seq_id":555}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"emissive":0}},"ref":"oxy","children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#02d1d1"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"D","auth_seq_id":555}},"children":[{"kind":"transform","params":{"translation":[0,0,0]},"ref":"oxyy"},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#02d1d1"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":0},"ref":"oxop"}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1myf.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"ref":"1myf","children":[{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"transform","params":{"translation":[0,0,0]}},{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"spacefill"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#d3a4a6"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":1},"ref":"spo"}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"backbone"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#d3a4a6"}}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"tooltip":"Click for next part","label_opacity":0,"label_background_color":"grey","snapshot_key":"end"},"ref":"next","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","position":[0,-25,0],"text":"Next Scene →","label_color":"white","label_size":5},"ref":"next_label"}]},{"kind":"camera","params":{"position":[1.94613295233414,0.7,77.67100787125258],"target":[-0.1,0.7,0.6],"up":[0,1,0]}}]},"metadata":{"key":"oxygen","title":"Oxygen Bound","description":"# Oxygen Bound to Myoglobin\n\nA later structure of myoglobin, PDB entry [1mbo](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/1mbo), \nshows that oxygen binds to the iron atom deep inside the protein. \nSo how does it get in and out? The \nanswer is that the structure in the PDB is only one snapshot of the \nprotein, caught when it is in a tightly-closed form. In reality, \nmyoglobin (and all other proteins) is constantly in motion, performing \nsmall flexing and breathing motions (illustrated here by PDB entry [1myf](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/1myf)). So, temporary openings constantly \nappear and disappear, allowing oxygen in and out.","linger_duration_ms":18000,"transition_duration_ms":500},"animation":{"kind":"animation","children":[{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"spo","duration_ms":5000,"start_ms":0,"property":"opacity","start":1,"end":0.05}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"1myf","start_ms":11000,"duration_ms":10000,"frequency":4,"alternate_direction":true,"property":"model_index","discrete":true,"start":0,"end":11}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"oxy","start_ms":3000,"duration_ms":10000,"frequency":7,"alternate_direction":true,"property":["custom","molstar_representation_params","emissive"],"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"vec3","target_ref":"oxyy","duration_ms":5000,"start_ms":16000,"property":"translation","frequency":4,"alternate_direction":false,"start":[5,-5,-20],"end":[0,0,0],"noise_magnitude":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"oxop","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":15000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"next","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":18000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}}],"params":{},"custom":{"molstar_trackball":{"name":"spin","params":{"speed":-0.05}}}}},{"root":{"kind":"root","custom":{"molstar_on_load_markdown_commands":{"play-audio":"AudioMOM1_D.mp3"}},"children":[{"kind":"download","params":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry-files/download/1mbn.bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"parse","params":{"format":"bcif"},"children":[{"kind":"structure","params":{"type":"model"},"children":[{"kind":"primitives","params":{"label_opacity":0},"ref":"dist","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"distance_measurement","start":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":44,"atom_id":356},"end":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":47,"atom_id":388},"radius":0.1,"dash_length":0.1,"label_size":2}},{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"distance_measurement","start":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":77,"atom_id":613},"end":{"label_asym_id":"A","auth_seq_id":18,"atom_id":149},"radius":0.1,"dash_length":0.1,"label_size":2}}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":[{"label_comp_id":"ALA"},{"label_comp_id":"VAL"},{"label_comp_id":"LEU"},{"label_comp_id":"ILE"},{"label_comp_id":"MET"},{"label_comp_id":"PHE"},{"label_comp_id":"TRP"},{"label_comp_id":"PRO"}]},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#bec0f2"}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":1},"ref":"carb"}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":[{"label_comp_id":"LYS"},{"label_comp_id":"ARG"},{"label_comp_id":"HIS"}]},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":"blue","saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":3}}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":1},"ref":"chargedp"}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":[{"label_comp_id":"ASP"},{"label_comp_id":"GLU"}]},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{},"custom":{"molstar_color_theme_name":"illustrative","molstar_color_theme_params":{"style":{"name":"uniform","params":{"value":"red","saturation":0,"lightness":0}},"carbonLightness":3}}},{"kind":"opacity","params":{"opacity":1},"ref":"chargedn"}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":{"label_asym_id":"A"}},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"backbone"},"children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"#919191"}}]}]},{"kind":"component","params":{"selector":"ligand"},"children":[{"kind":"representation","params":{"type":"ball_and_stick"},"custom":{"molstar_representation_params":{"emissive":0}},"ref":"ligand","children":[{"kind":"color","params":{"color":"orange"}}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"opacity":0.33},"ref":"salt1","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"ellipsoid","center":[22.75,32.65,-7.300000000000001],"major_axis":[0.8999999999999986,-1.2999999999999972,-2.2],"minor_axis":[-1.2999999999999972,-0.8999999999999986,0],"radius":[5,3,3],"color":"#cccccc"}}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"opacity":0.33},"ref":"salt2","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"ellipsoid","center":[15.350000000000001,23.05,21.35],"major_axis":[-2.5000000000000018,1.1000000000000014,1.6999999999999993],"minor_axis":[1.1000000000000014,2.5000000000000018,0],"radius":[5,3,3],"color":"#cccccc"}}]},{"kind":"primitives","params":{"tooltip":"Click for next part","label_opacity":0,"label_background_color":"grey","snapshot_key":"intro"},"ref":"next","children":[{"kind":"primitive","params":{"kind":"label","position":[13.5,-10,7.7],"text":"Next Scene →","label_color":"white","label_size":5},"ref":"next_label"}]},{"kind":"camera","params":{"position":[11.261562340189554,-4.330509550438595,-51.05581130024533],"target":[13.6,21.1,7.6],"up":[0.1,0.9,-0.4]}}]},"metadata":{"key":"end","title":"Conclusion","description":"# Molecule of the Month: Myoglobin\n\nThe atomic structure of myoglobin revealed many of the basic principles \nof protein structure and stability. For instance, the structure showed \nthat when the protein chain folds into a globular structure, \ncarbon-rich amino acids are sheltered \ninside and charged amino acids positively \nand negatively are most often found on the surface, \noccasionally forming salt bridges \nthat pair two opposite charges (shown here with circles). \n\nTo explore some of these principles, explore freely in the interactive view.\n\n## Topics for Further Discussion\n\nYou can use the sequence comparison tool to align the sequences of different \nmyoglobins, looking for mutations. For instance, [here is the alignment of whale and pig myoglobin](https://www.rcsb.org/alignment?request-body=eJyljrsOwjAMRf%2FFcxgqxNKN7kXsqKpC4pZIeZTEVamq%2FDtOGRAzm%2BPje3I3eM4YV6g3CBOZ4FMZI9IcfZ%2BQoVfYa0kS6kHahFmACp7wReXQBY1QwyRNXExCEOCQHkEX5qUrjNxBWjN64GSiOCtWI%2F9y2wA9xbU3fA1V21w4ndCiKjWKQKbVfeiZ0R3HUmhfVIKz%2Bvs8HXMWv75r2%2Fzn61gJg7F71y6%2FARZEZL8%3D&response-body=eJzlU11vmzAU%2FS88Q2RsjKFv7iCA7GRJQFRVVUU0uClSQjo%2BtkVV%2FvuuyUdTadMeurcJIXF97j33HN%2FLm1HVzzvj5s3o%2B6o0bgzlUaZoyaynwvUshznPll8UpVVgRUr1hAkrmWEabVd0fQv5X75OZjLMQuNgGlvVFZqq2FTreqvqbrndlQqSXouq%2BVG1CgqvMNW97HTLbmsNp5qiUW2%2F6YD44Q16NP2q6%2BFoCKGm2S8HkfbkdqpFqI1addWuHpq2%2B%2B0R5QA9qfWyVd%2BGA9uE2vI9pORwMD%2FyzSa3n%2BN7NN%2FlLi8eB92NWgOl9vDwF1YdVnWpfho3yDQ2ql53L0f%2BR%2FMTtaCta4q6fd4126I7a7FNdHp%2B%2BwUd0chxCXY9xjA2LTRiNkWMONT2TDSimDi%2Bz1yHQDaAmGCbeTbxXR25rodsG%2FvHiCGGEHE9D2vukUcpdgnBlEGAEfU9RrFPdKbDqOMT2x8yLYpH1MWOQxzP9U3CRi5lBCGKoKlFR77j2Rg5iNkgVw%2Bg326LZq%2BH165257X5Xmx62EFo68I97F%2F1PsK99apeKasqYUpVtzf0QlwyXeeSuZikwUfQ9y5gNrGGRoYefw1jr5fQtSp7tdQb3w73rxH9G2xUeUa1MI3Aq2XDEHUpzOxUoKPV7rtqirXSqQjmgdDjcctO0v%2B4ZJ%2FYsQs5lOYyDaPwbi5zGed3XOQhD3IexdE8SGSykGORxrMwk6EYB4uxiKXIQh5OBE%2FDQAoRR3mWy4zLiCcQiiiOAZZiJvk8jXkmYpHMEnEvw3GShjxJYuiTLuJZFIwjHvB5xCdTwWUoxwsRJJyLexHK6H4eDdP453YjmQYnu9P8LrqyG%2BZHu9HFrhjsgs9ru9OT3ejabvbBbn5ld57LeSo%2B2E1PdqfB5Gx3rO3%2BH5t9%2BAU7Kf5z&encoded=true) used to create the illustration in this column.\n\nPDB entry [2jho](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/2jho) includes myoglobin poisoned by cyanide. Take a look and you'll see that the cyanide blocks the binding site for oxygen.\n\n## References\n\n- 1mbn: J. C. Kendrew, R. E. Dickerson, B. E. Strandberg, R. G. Hart, D. R. Davies, D. C. Phillips & V. C. Shore (1960) Structure of Myoglobin. Nature 185, 422-427.\n- J. C. Kendrew (1961) The three-dimensional structure of a protein molecule. Scientific American 205(6), 96-110.\n- 1mbo: S. E. Phillips (1980) Structure and refinement of oxymyoglobin at 1.6 A resolution. Journal of Molecular Biology 142, 531-554.\n- 1pmb: S. J. Smerdon, T. J. Oldfield, E. J. Dodson, G. G. Dodson, R. E. Hubbard & A. J. Wilkinson (1990) Determination of the crystal structure of recombinant pig myoglobin by molecular replacement and its refinement. Acta Crystallographica B, 46, 370-377.\n- 1myf: Osapay K, Theriault Y, Wright PE, Case DA. Solution structure of carbonmonoxy myoglobin determined from nuclear magnetic resonance distance and chemical shift constraints. J Mol Biol. 1994;244(2):183-197. doi:10.1006/jmbi.1994.1718\n- S. Mirceta, A. V. Signore, J. M. Burns, A. R. Cossins, K. L. Campbell & M. Berenbrink (2013) Evolution of mammalian diving capacity traced by myoglobin net surface charge. Science 340, 1234192.","linger_duration_ms":20000,"transition_duration_ms":500},"animation":{"kind":"animation","children":[{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"carb","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":8000,"frequency":2,"alternate_direction":true,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"chargedp","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":10000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"chargedn","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":10000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"salt1","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":11000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":0.3}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"salt2","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":11000,"property":"opacity","start":0,"end":0.3}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"dist","duration_ms":1000,"start_ms":11000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}},{"kind":"interpolate","params":{"kind":"scalar","target_ref":"next","duration_ms":2000,"start_ms":20000,"property":"label_opacity","start":0,"end":1}}],"params":{}}}]}